1. Purpose

Test thorn for PlanesX's 2D plane output (extracted from CarpetX) (Silo and openPMD). It declares one
grid function per index-type centering (the eight V/C combinations) and fills
each with the same analytic, axis-distinguishing field

    f(x, y, z) = x + 100 y + 10000 z

evaluated at the grid function's own centering-dependent coordinate. The field
is linear so it is exactly representable on every refinement level after
prolongation/restriction.

The parfiles in test/ drive single-level and AMR runs that emit xy/xz/yz
planes (the three principal planes plus one off-centre elevation per
direction) through both the Silo and openPMD plane writers. The companion
script test/verify_planes.py reads the written plane files back, reconstructs
each point's world coordinate from the file metadata, and asserts that the
stored value equals f to within tolerance -- a rigorous, reference-free check
that the snap, slab extraction, axis ordering and per-centering coordinates
are all correct.

See PlanesX/doc/plane_output.md for the feature and test documentation.
